# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-only
# boot.part -- A moulded boot over either end of a chassis
# Copyright (c) 2026 Jakob Kastelic

# The frame: x across, z up, y back, the front face of the panel at
# y = 0.  A stack of profiles seen from the front: the sleeve round the
# chassis end, open at the bottom in a gap; the recess over the Lexan
# overlay; and the lip over the panel, round the lip opening.  The lip
# face rises into six bumpers, two on each side and two halves at each
# of the top and the bottom corners, in waves: the lip is what a tall
# extrusion of its profile has in common with two extrusions of a wavy
# outline, one along x and one along z.  So the outer edge of the front
# is one smooth closed run, and one round follows it.  Screw holes,
# counterbored for the heads, go through the side walls and through the
# top and bottom bands.
#
# The boot is made for a mould that opens along y and parts at PART_Y,
# PART_GAP behind the counterbores of the screws, so that every hole
# lies on faces without a draft.  The holes lie across the way the
# mould opens: side pins make them, or a drill.  Ahead of that plane
# the outside has no draft.  Behind it the outside leans in by
# BOOT_DRAFT_OUT, for a light texture, and the cavity opens by
# BOOT_DRAFT_FIT, so that the outside shows a crease all round on the
# parting line.  Slots and grooves cored from the rear, their walls
# drawn by BOOT_DRAFT_CORE, leave walls of about CW: they run along y in
# the inner faces of the sleeve and out at its rear end, and those under
# a bumper run on forward as pockets under it, whose floors follow the
# waves.  Seen from behind they make an even rhythm of slots and ribs
# round the rim.  The ribs bear on the chassis, and the walls stay whole
# round the screws.  The values come from the parameters of the chassis, in
# mm.  Build it with
#   extrude test/boot.part | bool - | fillet - | tostep - > boot.step

W = 339.09
H = 170.688
WALL = 6.35
FOOT = 5.65
TOP = 11
LIP = 7.62
POCKET_X0 = 65.1948
POCKET_X1 = 273.8952
COV_T = 1.6002
BEND_R = 0.762
BOOT_R = 12.7
SOFT_R = 1.016
OPEN_R = 3.81
LEXAN_X0 = 5.1522
LEXAN_X1 = 333.9378
LEXAN_Z1 = 165.7898
LEXAN_T = 0.3548
BOOT_L = 38.1
LIP_T = 3.81
BUMP_L = 25
BUMP_H = 9.34
BUMP_Z0 = 64.344
BUMP_Z1 = 125.144
SCREW_Y = 10.16
SCREW_DZ = 56.896
SLEEVE = 4.7625
HEAD = 7.62
HEAD_D = 2.54
BAND_X = 60
BAND_XB = 55

X0 = -WALL
X1 = W + WALL
Z0 = -WALL - FOOT
Z1 = H + TOP
XA = POCKET_X0 + 2 * COV_T
XB = POCKET_X1 - 2 * COV_T
RV = COV_T + BEND_R
LX0 = LEXAN_X0 - 0.2
LX1 = LEXAN_X1 + 0.2
LZ0 = LIP - OPEN_R
LZ1 = LEXAN_Z1 + 0.2
RL = 0.5
YR = BOOT_L - LIP_T
BOOT_DRAFT_OUT = 2
BOOT_DRAFT_FIT = 1
BOOT_DRAFT_CORE = 1.5
PART_GAP = 1.5
PART_Y = SCREW_Y + HEAD / 2 + PART_GAP

# The outer outline, then the cavity: its bottom corners sharp, for the
# square edges of the front plate; the top ones clear the outer bends of
# the top cover.
profile back along y XB Z0 0 X1 Z0 BOOT_R X1 Z1 BOOT_R X0 Z1 BOOT_R
corner X0 Z0 BOOT_R XA Z0 0
corner XA 0 RV 0 0 0 0 H SOFT_R W H SOFT_R W 0 0 XB 0 RV
profile lip along y XB Z0 0 X1 Z0 BOOT_R X1 Z1 BOOT_R X0 Z1 BOOT_R
corner X0 Z0 BOOT_R XA Z0 0
corner XA LIP OPEN_R LIP LIP OPEN_R LIP H-LIP OPEN_R W-LIP H-LIP OPEN_R
corner W-LIP LIP OPEN_R XB LIP OPEN_R
profile lipx along y XB Z0 0 X1 Z0 BOOT_R X1 Z1 BOOT_R X0 Z1 BOOT_R
corner X0 Z0 BOOT_R XA Z0 0
corner XA LZ0 0 LX0 LZ0 RL LX0 LZ1 RL LX1 LZ1 RL LX1 LZ0 RL XB LZ0 0

extrude sleeve from 0 to PART_Y back

# Behind the parting plane the outside leans in by BOOT_DRAFT_OUT, for a
# textured mould face, and the cavity opens by BOOT_DRAFT_FIT, so that
# the fit on the chassis stays close.  The chain from the outer bottom
# round the corners of the gap to the top of each band is smooth, so it
# takes one draft, that of the outside: rb has the outline of the
# outside and the gap, and fills the cavity but for a box over the gap,
# whose sides XG lie in the last slots of the bottom bands.  cav1, the
# cavity less that box, then cuts the cavity at BOOT_DRAFT_FIT.  It
# grows toward the rear from its outline at PART_Y, so it is drawn at
# YT, EF further out.  The corners of the gap are round in rb, for a
# sharp corner would turn at the parting line, and no ball rolls round
# that turn; the round shrinks with the draft.  XG is the middle of the
# last slot of each bottom band, below.
YT = YR+1
TF = tan(BOOT_DRAFT_FIT)
EF = (YT-PART_Y)*TF
XG = 61.57
ZC = H/2
profile outd along y XB Z0 SOFT_R X1 Z0 BOOT_R X1 Z1 BOOT_R X0 Z1 BOOT_R
corner X0 Z0 BOOT_R XA Z0 SOFT_R XA 0 RV XG 0 0 XG ZC 0 W-XG ZC 0
corner W-XG 0 0 XB 0 RV
profile cavd along y -EF -EF 0 XG+EF -EF 0 XG+EF ZC-EF 0 W-XG-EF ZC-EF 0
corner W-XG-EF -EF 0 W+EF -EF 0 W+EF H+EF SOFT_R+EF -EF H+EF SOFT_R+EF
extrude rb from PART_Y to YR outd draft BOOT_DRAFT_OUT
extrude cav1 from YT to PART_Y cavd draft BOOT_DRAFT_FIT
cut rear rb cav1
extrude recess from -LEXAN_T to 0 lipx

# The waves.  Seen from the side, pv, the front runs at the height of
# the bumpers, YB, for BLV from the top and from the bottom and between
# BUMP_Z0 and BUMP_Z1, and at the lip face, -LIP_T, between; seen from
# above, ph, at YB for BUMP_L from each side.  Each step is an S of two
# arcs, A1 where it turns outward and A2 where it turns inward.  Both
# outlines close behind the lip, at YE, and beyond the outer faces.
A1 = 5.6
A2 = 3.6
BLV = 30
YB = -LIP_T - BUMP_H
YE = 1
profile pv along x YE Z0-1 0 YE Z1+1 0 YB Z1+1 0 YB Z1-BLV A1
corner -LIP_T Z1-BLV A2 -LIP_T BUMP_Z1 A2 YB BUMP_Z1 A1 YB BUMP_Z0 A1
corner -LIP_T BUMP_Z0 A2 -LIP_T Z0+BLV A2 YB Z0+BLV A1 YB Z0-1 0
profile ph along z X0-1 YE 0 X0-1 YB 0 X0+BUMP_L YB A1 X0+BUMP_L -LIP_T A2
corner X1-BUMP_L -LIP_T A2 X1-BUMP_L YB A1 X1+1 YB 0 X1+1 YE 0
extrude tall from YB-1 to -LEXAN_T lip
extrude wv from X0-1 to X1+1 pv
extrude wh from Z0-1 to Z1+1 ph
common f1 tall wv
common front f1 wh
union bumped sleeve rear recess front

# The screw holes, each a sleeve hole from the outer face with a
# counterbore for the head.
ZS0 = H/2-SCREW_DZ
ZS1 = H/2+SCREW_DZ
circle side0 along x SCREW_Y ZS0 SLEEVE
circle side1 along x SCREW_Y ZS1 SLEEVE
circle head0 along x SCREW_Y ZS0 HEAD
circle head1 along x SCREW_Y ZS1 HEAD
extrude hl0 from X0 to 0 side0
extrude hl1 from X0 to 0 side1
extrude hr0 from W to X1 side0
extrude hr1 from W to X1 side1
extrude cl0 from X0 to X0+HEAD_D head0
extrude cl1 from X0 to X0+HEAD_D head1
extrude cr0 from X1-HEAD_D to X1 head0
extrude cr1 from X1-HEAD_D to X1 head1
circle top0 along z BAND_X SCREW_Y SLEEVE
circle top1 along z W-BAND_X SCREW_Y SLEEVE
circle tophead0 along z BAND_X SCREW_Y HEAD
circle tophead1 along z W-BAND_X SCREW_Y HEAD
circle bot0 along z BAND_XB SCREW_Y SLEEVE
circle bot1 along z W-BAND_XB SCREW_Y SLEEVE
circle bothead0 along z BAND_XB SCREW_Y HEAD
circle bothead1 along z W-BAND_XB SCREW_Y HEAD
extrude ht0 from H to Z1 top0
extrude ht1 from H to Z1 top1
extrude ct0 from Z1-HEAD_D to Z1 tophead0
extrude ct1 from Z1-HEAD_D to Z1 tophead1
extrude hb0 from Z0 to 0 bot0
extrude hb1 from Z0 to 0 bot1
extrude cb0 from Z0 to Z0+HEAD_D bothead0
extrude cb1 from Z0 to Z0+HEAD_D bothead1
cut holed bumped hl0 hl1 hr0 hr1 cl0 cl1 cr0 cr1 ht0 ht1 ct0 ct1 hb0 hb1 cb0 cb1

# The cores.  Each is an extrusion from YS, just behind the parting
# plane, toward the front, which shrinks by BOOT_DRAFT_CORE on the way,
# so the outlines below hold at YS and lie E1 further out than at y = 0.
# Behind YS the mouths, below, go on to YT, past the rear end.  CW is
# the wall left to the outside at y = 0: it thins toward the rear, as
# both its faces lean, to CW less YR TC and (YR - PART_Y) TO.  CL is the
# wall under the waves.
TC = tan(BOOT_DRAFT_CORE)
TO = tan(BOOT_DRAFT_OUT)
STEP = 0.5
YS = PART_Y+1
E1 = YS*TC
E0 = YT*TC
CW = 4.1
CL = 3.5

# The floors of the pockets: the waves moved in by CL, their steps
# leaning by SD.  ARC is the length of a step's inner arc along the lip.
SD = 2
SL = BUMP_H*tan(SD)
ARC = (A2+CL)*tan(45-SD/2)
YD = YB+CL
YL = -LIP_T+CL
ZT = Z1-BLV+CL
ZU = BUMP_Z1-CL
ZV = BUMP_Z0+CL
ZW = Z0+BLV-CL
XU = X0+BUMP_L-CL
X1U = X1-BUMP_L+CL
profile pvo along x YT+1 Z0-1 0 YT+1 Z1+1 0 YD Z1+1 0 YD ZT A1-CL
corner YL ZT-SL A2+CL YL ZU+SL A2+CL YD ZU A1-CL YD ZV A1-CL
corner YL ZV-SL A2+CL YL ZW+SL A2+CL YD ZW A1-CL YD Z0-1 0
profile pho along z X0-1 YT+1 0 X0-1 YD 0 XU YD A1-CL XU+SL YL A2+CL
corner X1U-SL YL A2+CL X1U YD A1-CL X1+1 YD 0 X1+1 YT+1 0
extrude wvo from X0-1 to X1+1 pvo
extrude who from Z0-1 to Z1+1 pho

# The rhythm of the slots, seen from behind.  Along each run the slots
# have one width and the ribs between them another, RIB at y = 0 on
# every run; each rib under a screw has the screw at its middle, and
# the slots lie the same way about the middle of the boot.  The four
# corner slots wrap round the corners of the cavity with two legs:
# LEG_S along the side walls, LEG_T along the top and the bottom bands,
# both about half a side slot.  On the side walls the ribs lie at the
# screws and at mid-height, with one slot between each pair, PS apart;
# on the top they lie PT apart, with the screws on the second and the
# ninth rib; on each bottom band two slots lie between the rib after
# the corner slot and the rib of the screw, and one beyond it.
# RIB is the least that leaves 2 mm of wall from a screw hole to the
# slots beside it.  Every slot has the round CR in its corners, and the
# corner slots CRK.  The end of a slot that runs on under a bumper lies
# GAP clear of the steps of its floor, as a round corner meets a step on
# no line or circle; CRK lets the ends of the corner slots on the side
# walls clear them.
RIB = 9.4
GAP = 0.12
CR0 = 1.5
CR = CR0+E1
CRK0 = 0.9
CRK = CRK0+E1
PS = SCREW_DZ
LEG_S = ZS0-RIB/2
PT = (W-2*BAND_X)/7
LEG_T = BAND_X-PT-RIB/2

# The corner slots, kbl to ktr, and the side slots, two along each side
# wall, ksl and ksr.  A slot reaches from CW inside the outer face to FIN
# short of the wall of the recess, across the back of the lip.  Two
# chords, with corners of RC, follow the outer corner round of the
# sleeve at CW; RCI is the corner inside the corner of the cavity, and
# CRP the corners of the legs there, which stay inside the cavity.
FIN = 1.4
RC = 2+E1
RCI = 1.2
CRP = RCI+E1
XO = X0+CW-E1
XI = LX0-FIN-E0+E1
ZO0 = Z0+CW-E1
ZI0 = LZ0-FIN-E0+E1
ZO1 = Z1-CW+E1
ZI1 = LZ1+FIN+E0-E1
RO = BOOT_R-CW+E1
S45 = sqrt(0.5)
CX = X0+BOOT_R
CZ0 = Z0+BOOT_R
CZ1 = Z1-BOOT_R
AX = CX-RO*S45
XE = LEG_T+E1
ZE = LEG_S+E1
ZF = H-LEG_S-E1
profile lbl along y XO CZ0 RC AX CZ0-RO*S45 RC CX ZO0 RC XE ZO0 CRK XE ZI0 CRP
corner XI ZI0 RCI XI ZE CRK XO ZE CRK
profile ltl along y XO ZF CRK XI ZF CRK XI ZI1 RCI XE ZI1 CRP XE ZO1 CRK
corner CX ZO1 RC AX CZ1+RO*S45 RC XO CZ1 RC
profile lbr along y W-XO CZ0 RC W-AX CZ0-RO*S45 RC W-CX ZO0 RC W-XE ZO0 CRK
corner W-XE ZI0 CRP W-XI ZI0 RCI W-XI ZE CRK W-XO ZE CRK
profile ltr along y W-XO ZF CRK W-XI ZF CRK W-XI ZI1 RCI W-XE ZI1 CRP
corner W-XE ZO1 CRK W-CX ZO1 RC W-AX CZ1+RO*S45 RC W-XO CZ1 RC
ZP0 = ZS0+RIB/2-E1
ZP1 = H/2-RIB/2+E1
profile psl along y XO ZP0 CR XI ZP0 CR XI ZP1 CR XO ZP1 CR
profile psr along y W-XO ZP0 CR W-XO ZP1 CR W-XI ZP1 CR W-XI ZP0 CR
extrude kbl from YS to YB lbl draft BOOT_DRAFT_CORE
extrude ktl from YS to YB ltl draft BOOT_DRAFT_CORE
extrude kbr from YS to YB lbr draft BOOT_DRAFT_CORE
extrude ktr from YS to YB ltr draft BOOT_DRAFT_CORE
extrude ksl from YS to YB psl draft BOOT_DRAFT_CORE pattern z 2 PS
extrude ksr from YS to YB psr draft BOOT_DRAFT_CORE pattern z 2 PS
union slots kbl ktl kbr ktr ksl ksr
common slotv slots wvo
common core slotv who

# The grooves of the top wall, nine, and of each bottom band, three, SB
# wide and PB apart, which leave no rib there thicker than RIB: they end
# flush with the back of the lip, at y = 0.
GT0 = LEG_T+RIB-E1
GT1 = BAND_X-RIB/2+E1
SB = (BAND_XB-RIB/2-LEG_T-2*RIB)/2
PB = SB+RIB
GB0 = LEG_T+RIB-E1
GB1 = LEG_T+RIB+SB+E1
GR0 = W-GB1-2*PB
GR1 = W-GB0-2*PB
profile pgt along y GT0 H-1 0 GT1 H-1 0 GT1 ZO1 CR GT0 ZO1 CR
profile pgb along y GB0 1 0 GB0 ZO0 CR GB1 ZO0 CR GB1 1 0
profile pgr along y GR0 1 0 GR0 ZO0 CR GR1 ZO0 CR GR1 1 0
extrude gt from YS to 0 pgt draft BOOT_DRAFT_CORE pattern x 9 PT
extrude gbl from YS to 0 pgb draft BOOT_DRAFT_CORE pattern x 3 PB
extrude gbr from YS to 0 pgr draft BOOT_DRAFT_CORE pattern x 3 PB

# The mouths.  Behind YS each slot and groove is STEP wider on each side
# that meets the cavity, so that the edges along the cavity there,
# which take RIM_R, end on the step at YS and cross no crease.  Ahead of
# YS those edges stay sharp.  The outlines hold at YT: those of the
# cores at YS moved out by DM, each side along its normal, with the
# step.  So a corner of two chords lies RQM from the centre of the
# outer round along their middle, and a chord meets a straight side
# DM T11 from where it met it before.
DM = E0-E1
XOM = XO-DM
ZO0M = ZO0-DM
ZO1M = ZO1+DM
ROM = RO+DM
T11 = tan(11.25)
RQM = (RO*cos(22.5)+DM)/cos(22.5)*S45
XEM = XE+DM+STEP
ZEM = ZE+DM+STEP
ZFM = ZF-DM-STEP
CRM = CR+DM
CRKM = CRK+DM
XIM = XI+DM
ZI0M = ZI0+DM
ZI1M = ZI1-DM
RCIM = RCI-DM
RCM = RC+DM
CRPM = CRP+DM
ZP0M = ZP0-DM-STEP
ZP1M = ZP1+DM+STEP
GT0M = GT0-DM-STEP
GT1M = GT1+DM+STEP
GB0M = GB0-DM-STEP
GB1M = GB1+DM+STEP
GR0M = GR0-DM-STEP
GR1M = GR1+DM+STEP
profile lblm along y XOM CZ0-DM*T11 RCM CX-RQM CZ0-RQM RCM CX-DM*T11 ZO0M RCM
corner XEM ZO0M CRKM
corner XEM ZI0M CRPM XIM ZI0M RCIM XIM ZEM CRKM XOM ZEM CRKM
profile ltlm along y XOM ZFM CRKM XIM ZFM CRKM XIM ZI1M RCIM XEM ZI1M CRPM
corner XEM ZO1M CRKM CX-DM*T11 ZO1M RCM CX-RQM CZ1+RQM RCM
corner XOM CZ1+DM*T11 RCM
profile lbrm along y W-XOM CZ0-DM*T11 RCM W-CX+RQM CZ0-RQM RCM
corner W-CX+DM*T11 ZO0M RCM
corner W-XEM ZO0M CRKM W-XEM ZI0M CRPM W-XIM ZI0M RCIM W-XIM ZEM CRKM
corner W-XOM ZEM CRKM
profile ltrm along y W-XOM ZFM CRKM W-XIM ZFM CRKM W-XIM ZI1M RCIM
corner W-XEM ZI1M CRPM W-XEM ZO1M CRKM W-CX+DM*T11 ZO1M RCM
corner W-CX+RQM CZ1+RQM RCM W-XOM CZ1+DM*T11 RCM
profile pslm along y XOM ZP0M CRM XIM ZP0M CRM XIM ZP1M CRM
corner XOM ZP1M CRM
profile psrm along y W-XOM ZP0M CRM W-XOM ZP1M CRM W-XIM ZP1M CRM
corner W-XIM ZP0M CRM
profile pgtm along y GT0M H-1 0 GT1M H-1 0 GT1M ZO1M CRM
corner GT0M ZO1M CRM
profile pgbm along y GB0M 1 0 GB0M ZO0M CRM GB1M ZO0M CRM GB1M 1 0
profile pgrm along y GR0M 1 0 GR0M ZO0M CRM GR1M ZO0M CRM GR1M 1 0
extrude mbl from YT to YS lblm draft BOOT_DRAFT_CORE
extrude mtl from YT to YS ltlm draft BOOT_DRAFT_CORE
extrude mbr from YT to YS lbrm draft BOOT_DRAFT_CORE
extrude mtr from YT to YS ltrm draft BOOT_DRAFT_CORE
extrude msl from YT to YS pslm draft BOOT_DRAFT_CORE pattern z 2 PS
extrude msr from YT to YS psrm draft BOOT_DRAFT_CORE pattern z 2 PS
extrude mgt from YT to YS pgtm draft BOOT_DRAFT_CORE pattern x 9 PT
extrude mgbl from YT to YS pgbm draft BOOT_DRAFT_CORE pattern x 3 PB
extrude mgbr from YT to YS pgrm draft BOOT_DRAFT_CORE pattern x 3 PB
union mouths mbl mtl mbr mtr msl msr mgt mgbl mgbr
cut boot holed core gt gbl gbr mouths

# The rounds.  Every edge that turns outward takes SOFT_R, but: the
# outer edge of the front, where the waves meet the outer faces, EDGE_R,
# up to the walls of the gap, the sides 9 and 19 of the profile; the
# rear edge of the lip opening on the ceiling of the recess, RECESS_R;
# every edge of the rear end, and the edges of the slots and grooves
# along the cavity behind the parting plane, RIM_R, so that the round of
# the rim runs on round each rib and into each mouth, three rounds meet
# in a ball at each corner of a rib, and each edge along the cavity
# ends on the cavity face at the parting plane; the front ends of the
# grooves, FLOOR_R in their inner corners; and the edges that stay
# sharp.  RIM_R is less than
# the round of the corners of the gap at the rear end, SOFT_R less the
# lean of the outside there.  Those that stay sharp are the edges hidden
# in use: of the face against the panel, the two short ones where the
# recess meets the gap, the inner edges of the counterbore floors, under
# the screw heads, and the edges of the slots and grooves along the
# cavity ahead of the parting plane, a round across which would meet the
# crease on no line or circle; the creases on the parting line; and the two
# ends of the sleeve's front part at the gap, which the rounds of its
# corners take whole.
RECESS_R = 0.3
EDGE_R = 5.08
RIM_R = 0.3
FLOOR_R = 1.2
round SOFT_R convex
round EDGE_R sleeve.back.* wv.*
round EDGE_R sleeve.back.* wh.*
round SOFT_R sleeve.back.9 wh.*
round SOFT_R sleeve.back.19 wh.*
round RECESS_R tall.end *
round RIM_R rb.end *
round RIM_R m* cav1.*
round RIM_R m* rb.*
sharp m*.end *
sharp k* cav1.*
sharp g* cav1.*
sharp g* rb.outd.*
sharp k* sleeve.back.*
sharp g* sleeve.back.*
sharp sleeve.back.* rb.*
sharp sleeve.back.* cav1.*
sharp sleeve.end *
sharp tall.end recess.lipx.*
sharp recess.end *
sharp sleeve.back.9 recess.lipx.*
sharp sleeve.back.19 recess.lipx.*
sharp cl*.end hl*
sharp cr*.start hr*
sharp ct*.start ht*
sharp cb*.end hb*
round FLOOR_R recess.end g*
